# Build output
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/

# Publish output - rebuilt by publish.ps1, and a 64 MB binary has no business
# in history.
MediaScout4-App/
MediaScout4-Release/

# The decompiled 3.x tree. Kept locally as a behavioural reference only: it is
# derived from a binary whose project carries no licence, so it must never be
# committed or distributed.
MediaScout-v3/Decompile/

# The original 3.x source clones. Unlicensed upstream, and each already has its
# own .git - they are reference material, not part of this project.
MediaScout/
MediaScout-v3/

# The original 3.x compiled application. Someone else's binary, under no licence
# that permits redistribution - never commit it.
MediaScout-App/

# Kodi scraper add-ons pulled down purely to read how they query the APIs.
kodi-reference/

# Local scratch
*.log
*.tmp

# Published output - rebuilt on demand, 64 MB, not source
PyreMedia.NET/publish/

# Kept builds. The .exe stays out of history - 64 MB is permanent once committed
# and cannot be pruned without rewriting it. Losing nothing by it: builds are
# deterministic (verified - a clean rebuild reproduces the same SHA-256), so the
# committed .sha256 beside each release is enough to rebuild that exact binary
# from its tag and prove it matches.
releases/**/*.exe

# publish.ps1's working output. The copy that matters is kept under releases/.
PyreMedia-Release/
PyreMedia-Release-Small/

# API keys. A working build carries its owner's keys in a file beside the exe
# rather than in the source, because a key in the repository is public the
# moment the repository is, whatever is deleted afterwards. This tree is the
# published one and should never hold such a file at all - the rule is here so
# that copying a working build across cannot quietly stage one.
keys.local.json
**/keys.local.json
# Working notes. The public repository carries documentation, not the record of
# how it got built - and a file of half-finished thoughts is the easiest way for
# something private to reach it by accident.
TODO.md
BLURB.md
docs/BLURB.md
next.md
